    fix(sim): prevent weak AICPU symbols from polluting HOST .so global table (#211)
    
    In a2a3sim, HOST .so is loaded with RTLD_GLOBAL via Python ctypes.
    The weak fallback `get_sys_cnt_aicpu()` (returns 0) in pto_orchestrator.cpp
    was being exported into the global dynamic symbol table.  When AICPU .so
    was subsequently loaded with RTLD_NOW|RTLD_GLOBAL, its PLT entries resolved
    to the HOST .so's weak symbol instead of its own strong definition from
    device_time.cpp, causing dispatch_time and finish_time in profiling records
    to always be 0.
    
    Add `visibility("hidden")` to both weak fallbacks so HOST .so does not
    export them globally.  This causes the AICPU .so's internal calls to bypass
    the PLT entirely and call the strong local definition directly.
    
    Also strengthen the dcci() simulation macro from memory_order_acquire to
    memory_order_seq_cst (dmb ish) to cover the flush/write-back direction:
    acquire fences do not prevent store-store reordering on aarch64, which
    could allow the AICPU to observe the FIN signal before perf_buf->count
    is visible.
    
    Co-authored-by: zhusy54 <zhusiyu1@hisilicon.com>

