Author: Chao Wang <26245345+ChaoWao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Feb 28 23:08:05 2026 +0800

    Fix: count implicitly completed running tasks in pipelined dispatch (#145)
    
    The host_build_graph AICPU executor uses a running/pending two-stage
    pipeline: while a running task executes on AICore, the next task can be
    dispatched as pending. When AICore finishes faster than AICPU polls the
    COND register, the running task's FIN is overwritten by the pending
    task's ACK or FIN, causing AICPU to never observe the running task's
    completion.
    
    The code already resolved the running task's downstream dependencies in
    this case, but forgot to increment completed_tasks_ and
    cur_thread_completed. This caused the scheduler to stall at N-M/N
    (e.g., 125/128) waiting for tasks that were actually done.
    
    Fix both Case 1 (pending FIN) and Case 2 (pending ACK) to count the
    implicitly completed running task.

