    Fix: use SEQ_CST ordering to prevent IRIW hazard on ARM (#122)
    
    Upgrade four atomic operations from ACQ_REL/ACQUIRE/RELEASE to SEQ_CST
    to close an IRIW (Independent Reads of Independent Writes) race between
    the scheduler and orchestrator threads on ARM:
    
      Scheduler:    fetch_add(refcount)  → load(fanin_count)
      Orchestrator: store(fanin_count)   → load(refcount)
    
    With ACQ_REL, ARM allows both threads to simultaneously see stale values,
    leaving a consumer task stuck forever. SEQ_CST guarantees a single total
    order so at least one thread observes the other's write.

