    Fix paged attention correctness for partial last blocks
    
    Previously the softmax_prepare kernel assumed all blocks were fully
    populated (valid_len == block_size). When context_len is not a multiple
    of block_size, the last block contains garbage values in columns
    [valid_len, block_size), which corrupt the softmax output and produce
    incorrect attention weights.
    
    Changes:
    - aiv_softmax_prepare: add TFILLPAD_INPLACE masking that fills columns
      [valid_len, N) with -inf before scaling, so exp(-inf)=0 zeroes out
      invalid key positions. Uses dynamic-cols TileSijDyn to mark the valid
      boundary and PadValue::Min TileSijPad for the fill value.
    - paged_attention_orch: compute valid_len = min(block_size, seq_len -
      bn * block_size) per block and pass it as an 8th arg to the softmax
      prepare task.
    - golden.py: change context_len from 8192 to non-aligned values (8100,
      8150) so the golden reference exercises partial-block paths.
    
    Applied to both aicpu_build_graph and host_build_graph test variants.
    
