Author: ChaoZheng109 <zhengchao47@huawei.com>
Date:   Fri Jan 30 11:21:45 2026 +0800

    Fix: Ensure timeout detection executes when all cores busy
    
    Problem:
    - When cur_thread_tasks_in_flight >= core_num, continue statement skipped Phase 2
    - This also skipped timeout detection code after Phase 2
    - If a task hung (infinite loop/livelock), idle_iterations never incremented
    - Timeout mechanism completely failed, system hung with no diagnostic output
    
    Root Cause:
    - continue jumps to next iteration, bypassing all code after it
    - Timeout detection placed after the continue statement
    
    Solution:
    - Change: if (busy) { continue } Phase2 Timeout
    - To:     if (!busy) { Phase2 } Timeout (always runs)
    - Phase 2 now conditionally executed instead of skipped
    - Timeout detection always runs in every loop iteration
    
    Impact:
    - Timeout can now detect hung tasks even when cores fully loaded
    - Diagnostic reports will trigger correctly for livelock scenarios
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

